-- title:
--   Unramified-outside-S replacement for a Hecke–Galois datum
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation domain (adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $T$ be a complete noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with local structure map, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Assume $p$ is prime, $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, $p\in S$, and every prime dividing $N$ lies in $S$. Given a datum $H$ consisting of a ring map $\pi:\mathrm{Hecke}\to T$ whose residues recover $\theta$, with $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{im}\pi]=T$, with every $\mathcal{O}$-valued lift $\chi$ of $\theta$ factoring as $\psi\circ\pi$ for an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi:T\to\mathcal{O}$, with $\mathcal{O}\to T\to T/\mathfrak{m}_T$ surjective, together with a rank-$2$ free adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, are $X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible, the conclusion is that some datum $H'$ for the same $(N,S,\mathcal{O},\theta,T)$ satisfies $H'.\pi=H.\pi$ and has $H'.\rho$ unramified at every prime $q\notin S$: for every valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$, all elements of its inertia subgroup act trivially.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura–Deligne–Carayol statement that the Galois representation attached to a Hecke eigensystem of level $N$ and residue characteristic $p$ is unramified outside the primes dividing $Np$, here in the form: a Hecke–Galois datum may be replaced by one with the same Hecke structure map whose representation is unramified outside $S$. It is used by [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isUnramifiedAt_of_notMem`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isUnramifiedAt_of_notMem).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum_exists_pi_eq_and_forall_isUnramifiedAt.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

variable {p : ℕ} {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] {S : Finset ℕ}
  {𝒪 : Type} [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
  [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
  {θ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S : Set ℕ) →+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪}
  {T : Type} [CommRing T] [IsLocalRing T] [IsNoetherianRing T]
  [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T) T] [Algebra 𝒪 T] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap 𝒪 T)]
  [Module.Finite 𝒪 T] [Module.Free 𝒪 T]

theorem CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_forall_isUnramifiedAt (hp : p.Prime)
    (hp𝒪 : (p : 𝒪) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) (hpS : p ∈ S)
    (hNS : ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∣ N → q ∈ S)
    (H : CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N (↑S : Set ℕ) 𝒪 θ T) :
    ∃ H' : CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N (↑S : Set ℕ) 𝒪 θ T, H'.π = H.π ∧
      ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∉ S → H'.ρ.IsUnramifiedAt q := by sorry
